    "halshs-05431314": {
      "title_s": [
        "EXCAVATIONS AT CHANHU-DARO, SINDH, 2019-2022"
      ],
      "abstract_s": [
        "Since 2016, the extensive excavation at Mound II, Chanhu-daro, has made it possible to document, for the very first time in the lower Indus Valley and over a very large area (6,500 m\u00b2), a planned city built of mud brick dated from the first centuries of the Indus Civilization (2600/2500-2300 BCE). Another major result of the 2015-2022 campaigns is the discovery, in most of the excavated neighborhoods, of craft workshops specialized in lapidary working."
      ],
      "halId_s": "halshs-05431314",
